{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Live host measurement 2026-09-06 01:29-01:32Z: sizing redone from data, two findings\n\n### The deploy-path finding is confirmed from the live host, not just from the source\n\n`docker ps` names the running containers `rebar-mcp-8e14d667da28-8092`,\n`compose-review-bot-1`, `compose-gerrit-1`, `compose-opcert-1`. The `<image>-<sha>-<port>`\nshape is `mcp_run_new`'s naming; the other three carry compose's own `compose-<service>-1`.\n**So the live host independently confirms what the source said: mcp does not come from\ncompose, and a compose-only `mem_limit` would never have bound it.** Every container also\nreports its limit as `7.631GiB` — the host total — which is docker's way of saying no limit\nis set on any of the four today.\n\n### Measurements\n\n`docker stats --no-stream` (instantaneous, 01:29Z) against CloudWatch\n`container_memory_rss_bytes` over 00:47-01:32Z:\n\n| service | docker stats 01:29Z | CW 45-min avg | CW 45-min max |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| mcp | **2941 MiB** | 1202 MiB | 2214 MiB |\n| review-bot | 629 MiB | 1023 MiB | **1886 MiB** (gate active) |\n| gerrit | 639 MiB | 696 MiB | 795 MiB |\n| opcert | 41 MiB | 41 MiB | 41 MiB |\n\nHost: `free -m` total **7813 MiB**, used 4796, **available 2615 (33.5%)**. Container total\n4250 MiB, so non-container use is ~516 MiB. Gate costs, measured: `plan_review` ~714 MB peak\n(748 MB observed on a local run tonight), `completion_verifier` 418-474 MB across ten samples.\n\nCorrections to the plan's stated numbers: host total is **7813 MiB, not 7987**; mcp's quiet\nbaseline is **not** ~0.97 GB — it is 2.2-2.9 GiB right now.\n\n### Finding 1 — the measurement justifies `max_concurrent_gates = 2` directly\n\nAgainst the measured 2615 MiB available:\n\n| permitted concurrency | worst-case plan-review demand | available after |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4 (today's code default) | 2856 MiB | **-241 MiB — exhausts memory** |\n| 2 (this change) | 1428 MiB | 1187 MiB |\n| 1 | 714 MiB | 1901 MiB |\n\n**Today's default of 4 cannot be satisfied by the memory the host actually has.** Two leaves\n1187 MiB, just above the 1024 MiB admission floor — so a third gate would be refused by the\nfloor even if the counter permitted it. That is why 2 and the floor belong together: the count\nis a static upper bound, the floor is what adapts to the host's real state. FALSIFIABLE CLAIM:\nwith no more than 2 slots held, available memory stays above 1024 MiB. DISPROOF: a\n`GATE_CONGESTED` refusal citing low memory while fewer than 2 slots are held.\n\n### Finding 2 — deliverable 2 as briefed is UNSATISFIABLE at current steady state, and I am not going to paper over it\n\nSizing each service for its measured steady state plus one concurrent gate, and honouring\ngerrit's configured 3 GiB reservation as instructed:\n\n    gerrit      3072 MiB   (configured reservation; it actually uses 639-795)\n    mcp         3655 MiB   (2941 steady + 714 gate)\n    review-bot  1343 MiB   (629 steady + 714 gate)\n    opcert       256 MiB\n    ----------------------\n    sum         8326 MiB   against a 7813 MiB host — over by 513 MiB, before any OS headroom\n\nThere is no allocation of these four that both covers current usage and leaves the host room.\nThe binding constraint is mcp's 2.9 GiB steady state, which alone is 38% of the box.\n\nThree ways out, and the choice is the operator's, not mine:\n\n- **A. Trim gerrit to 2560m.** Its 3 GiB figure sums an anonymous heap ceiling (`heapLimit 2g`)\n  with a *reclaimable* mmap window (`packedGitLimit 1g`); cgroup v2 evicts mapped file pages\n  under pressure rather than OOM-killing on them, so the binding anonymous demand is heap plus\n  ~512 MiB of JVM non-heap. Measured use is 639-795 MiB, giving 3.2x headroom at 2560m. This\n  DEPARTS from the brief's \"do not set gerrit below 3 GiB\", which is why it is flagged rather\n  than done. Even so the sum only reaches 7814 MiB — the host exactly, with no OS headroom.\n- **B. Treat the limits as ceilings, not reservations.** cgroup `memory.max` reserves nothing,\n  so a sum above RAM is ordinary practice provided EXPECTED CONCURRENT demand stays below RAM\n  — which is exactly what `max_concurrent_gates = 2` plus the 1024 MiB floor enforce. This\n  contradicts the brief's literal \"their sum plus OS overhead fits the host with room\", so it\n  needs an explicit decision.\n- **C. Resize the host.** This arithmetic is direct evidence for that decision rather than\n  against it.\n\n### Recorded, not settled: CPU is the acute pressure right now\n\nLoad average 4.69 / 4.99 / 5.08 on 2 vCPU is ~2.5x oversubscribed while memory sits at 33.5%\navailable. Recorded because it bears on the pending instance-family choice, and explicitly NOT\ntreated as settling it: this reading is from BEFORE any of this bounding lands."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788658390239817001,"uuid":"94caaf9b-59bf-425d-a791-86d90fdbaa92"}